{
 "id": "threads/model-switch-unreported/row1-change-stops",
 "description": "Main runs on the large model, and cmdfilter shrinks messages[9] from 8,000 to 1,000 tokens. On the next request the client moves to the small model and appends one message, and the host does not apply cmdfilter. The forwarded body differs from the previous one at messages[9], inside the cached prefix and before the client's first difference: design 5.2 row 1. No operation reports the model change, and the provider keeps a cache for each model, so nothing is read and all 38,500 tokens are written. The client body misses too, so the break is in the baseline, labelled model_changed: the 38,000 tokens of the prefix up to messages[9], from read to write, net out. Before accountant#69, row 1 booked it as a charged break with no ChangeID, which a host shows as an ended change.",
 "source": "issue_cases.md#69",
